;; Which shared security controls this repository actually reaches for.
;;
;; Written 2026-08-22, when grant became its own repository (root
;; ADR-2608219500). aiueos had a record like this; grant inherited the code
;; that exercised most of it and, for a day, none of the record.
;;
;; It is not a declaration. `grant.tcb/validate` reads every namespace named
;; below and checks that it really does require every control listed against
;; it, and that `:required-control-namespaces` is exactly the union of them.
;; A control that stops being used, or an entrypoint that quietly starts using
;; a new one, fails the suite. That is the difference between this file and a
;; comment.
{:adoption/version 2
 :consumer/id :grant
 :security/git-sha "49fc4ce359752e9fe6e547e9071b5b9b40da937a"
 :required-control-namespaces
 [kotoba.security.abac
  kotoba.security.crypto-policy
  kotoba.security.hardware
  kotoba.security.information-flow
  kotoba.security.redaction
  kotoba.security.supply-chain
  kotoba.security.transport]
 :security-sensitive-entrypoints
 {grant.policy [kotoba.security.abac
                kotoba.security.crypto-policy
                kotoba.security.hardware
                kotoba.security.information-flow
                kotoba.security.transport]
  grant.audit [kotoba.security.redaction]
  grant.deployment-profile [kotoba.security.supply-chain]}
 :exceptions []}
